    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Provider: AWS S3**\n\nI've decided to use `boto3` for AWS S3. It's a prevalent and recognizable choice, which should make the code more accessible and easier to understand for others. The focus is now on how to integrate `boto3` into the `list_prefix.py` script.\n\n\n**Defining Implementation Details**\n\nI'm now fully committed to integrating `boto3` within `list_prefix.py`. The core task will involve writing the S3 prefix listing logic, utilizing `boto3` functions. This means coding the `import boto3` statements, and configuring a client. I am moving towards writing the core of the `list_prefix.py` implementation.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789820499667,
          "start": 1789820498568
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b99d7288001F3I7QIFEOkq2Kz",
      "message_id": "msg_0b99d6cfb001AoPjXQg73SUIja",
      "session_id": "ses_f46629310ffeizwGojliMqBk9B",
      "time_created": 1789820498568,
      "time_updated": 1789820499667
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "Z0nOXUQ9aO52uW9X",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import boto3\n\ndef list_objects_with_prefix(bucket_name, prefix):\n    s3 = boto3.client('s3')\n    response = s3.list_objects_v2(Bucket=bucket_name, Prefix=prefix)\n    \n    if 'Contents' in response:\n        for obj in response['Contents']:\n            print(obj['Key'])\n    else:\n        print(f\"No objects found with prefix '{prefix}' in bucket '{bucket_name}'\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Replace with your bucket name and prefix\n    bucket = \"your-s3-bucket-name\" \n    prefix = \"your-prefix/\" \n    list_objects_with_prefix(bucket, prefix)\n",
            "filePath": "list_prefix.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
